# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-F5). L §3.6 Its split: "Parties whose remainders tie go by the owned clause's ties by e ...;
# a tie with none is refused (RUN-TIE, §5.13) ... The hole part of hole shares ranks after every party, so a known share
# is never lost to a hole." 1.01 PLN by ania's half and the hole part of tomek's unknown share: the remainders tie at
# the last cent, which goes to ania, with no ties by (ania 0.51, a hole part of 0.50; scratch/expf.py).  Its only
# possible owner is tomek, so of tomek reads 0.50 (L §8.1, 2.1-F12; was a HOLE-PART before 2.1-F12).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
input half: num
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania_tomek then 0 else 1
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_day: date
input wage_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then half else 0
  rule unknown beats base = ?"what share is tomek's" when p == tomek
move wage: transfers
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount wage_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania_tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  half = 0.5
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  wage_day = 2026-02-01
  wage_amt = 1.01 PLN
=== expect
q: (1.01 PLN, 0.51 PLN, 0.50 PLN, 0.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
